{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\Books\\6th\\Math\\JPG\\083.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "4.4Ratio", "conf": 0.846, "box": [[807, 89], [997, 86], [998, 128], [807, 130]]}, {"text": "We frequently come across situations like: \"Fahad's", "conf": 0.913, "box": [[194, 158], [981, 160], [981, 210], [193, 208]]}, {"text": "Math History", "conf": 0.883, "box": [[1060, 149], [1242, 148], [1242, 182], [1061, 183]]}, {"text": "Abu Rayhan Al-Biruni (973-1048 AD), a", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[1032, 200], [1530, 196], [1531, 239], [1033, 244]]}, {"text": "age is two times Mustafa's age\" or \"this pen is", "conf": 0.909, "box": [[196, 220], [907, 220], [907, 264], [196, 264]]}, {"text": "Muslim Mathematician, made a significant", "conf": 0.939, "box": [[1033, 240], [1576, 242], [1576, 282], [1032, 280]]}, {"text": "twice as costly as the other one\". In such situations,", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[194, 276], [983, 277], [983, 317], [194, 316]]}, {"text": "contribution to the field of arithmetic,", "conf": 0.934, "box": [[1032, 281], [1517, 277], [1518, 317], [1033, 321]]}, {"text": "particularly irrational numbers, ratio and", "conf": 0.944, "box": [[1032, 323], [1550, 317], [1551, 357], [1033, 364]]}, {"text": "we are actually comparing one thing, quantity or", "conf": 0.937, "box": [[195, 334], [948, 333], [948, 373], [195, 375]]}, {"text": "proportion.", "conf": 0.899, "box": [[1034, 370], [1183, 362], [1184, 396], [1036, 404]]}, {"text": "number with the other.", "conf": 0.899, "box": [[201, 388], [564, 394], [564, 427], [200, 422]]}, {"text": "There is another way to compare quantities which is called \"ratio\" We can say that the ratio", "conf": 0.92, "box": [[194, 432], [1603, 425], [1603, 478], [195, 485]]}, {"text": "of Fahad's age to Mustafa's age is 2 : 1. Here 2 and 1 are the terms of the ratio. We read this", "conf": 0.911, "box": [[197, 483], [1602, 478], [1602, 527], [198, 533]]}, {"text": "ratio as 2 is to 1.", "conf": 0.901, "box": [[200, 542], [464, 542], [464, 575], [200, 575]]}, {"text": "A term that is used to compare two or more quantities of the", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[195, 591], [1141, 589], [1141, 636], [196, 638]]}, {"text": "Previous Knowledge Check", "conf": 0.92, "box": [[1184, 597], [1592, 601], [1591, 637], [1184, 633]]}, {"text": "same kind is called \"Ratio\". Symbol \":\" is used to represent a", "conf": 0.901, "box": [[197, 644], [1120, 645], [1120, 686], [197, 685]]}, {"text": "How can we find how much", "conf": 0.868, "box": [[1243, 662], [1602, 663], [1602, 694], [1243, 693]]}, {"text": "ratio.", "conf": 0.762, "box": [[197, 697], [286, 697], [286, 733], [197, 733]]}, {"text": "one quantity is more than", "conf": 0.891, "box": [[1243, 704], [1591, 705], [1591, 735], [1243, 734]]}, {"text": "In general, If a and b are any two quantities of the same kind,", "conf": 0.923, "box": [[195, 747], [1146, 744], [1146, 786], [196, 789]]}, {"text": "the other quantity?", "conf": 0.869, "box": [[1243, 742], [1495, 742], [1495, 775], [1243, 775]]}, {"text": "How canwecomparetwo", "conf": 0.923, "box": [[1243, 780], [1582, 783], [1582, 814], [1243, 810]]}, {"text": "then a : b is called the ratio between a and b. It is read as a is", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[198, 799], [1138, 797], [1138, 834], [199, 836]]}, {"text": "or more quantities?", "conf": 0.883, "box": [[1246, 822], [1501, 818], [1502, 850], [1246, 853]]}, {"text": "to b. The quantities a and b are called the terms of the ratio.", "conf": 0.947, "box": [[197, 852], [1132, 848], [1132, 884], [198, 888]]}, {"text": "The first term of the ratio \"a\" is called the antecedent and the second term \"b\" is called the", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[199, 905], [1594, 898], [1594, 934], [200, 941]]}, {"text": "consequent. Look at these pencils and books.", "conf": 0.911, "box": [[199, 957], [915, 952], [915, 989], [200, 994]]}, {"text": "There are 7 pencils and 4 books. The ratio of the number of pencils to the number of books", "conf": 0.92, "box": [[214, 1149], [1605, 1136], [1605, 1179], [215, 1191]]}, {"text": "can be expressed as 7: 4 or7is to 4. Here, 7is the antecedent and 4 is the consequent.", "conf": 0.923, "box": [[216, 1205], [1528, 1194], [1529, 1234], [217, 1245]]}, {"text": "to", "conf": 0.633, "box": [[877, 1292], [918, 1292], [918, 1330], [877, 1330]]}, {"text": "Number of pencils", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[351, 1297], [645, 1292], [646, 1333], [351, 1337]]}, {"text": "Number of books", "conf": 0.822, "box": [[1152, 1292], [1417, 1290], [1417, 1324], [1152, 1326]]}, {"text": "Also, the ratio of the number of books to the number of pencils can be expressed as", "conf": 0.938, "box": [[202, 1372], [1495, 1360], [1496, 1405], [203, 1418]]}, {"text": "4 : 7 or 4 is to 7.", "conf": 0.908, "box": [[204, 1433], [461, 1427], [461, 1462], [205, 1467]]}, {"text": "to", "conf": 0.511, "box": [[878, 1466], [921, 1466], [921, 1503], [878, 1503]]}, {"text": "Number of pencils", "conf": 0.853, "box": [[1151, 1465], [1432, 1462], [1433, 1502], [1151, 1505]]}, {"text": "Number of books", "conf": 0.855, "box": [[353, 1475], [633, 1468], [634, 1502], [353, 1509]]}, {"text": "Here, 4 is the antecedent and 7 is the consequent. Hence, when we change the order of a", "conf": 0.937, "box": [[220, 1565], [1598, 1547], [1599, 1597], [221, 1615]]}, {"text": "ratio, the result will be changed. The following important points must be kept in mind", "conf": 0.948, "box": [[219, 1613], [1598, 1596], [1599, 1650], [220, 1666]]}, {"text": "while solving ratio related problems.", "conf": 0.92, "box": [[225, 1677], [795, 1660], [796, 1697], [226, 1714]]}, {"text": " The two quantities must be of the same kind.", "conf": 0.917, "box": [[296, 1719], [1044, 1701], [1045, 1744], [297, 1762]]}, {"text": "Ratio has no units.", "conf": 0.895, "box": [[313, 1774], [630, 1763], [631, 1797], [314, 1807]]}, {"text": "'manipulations.", "conf": 0.853, "box": [[352, 1894], [556, 1885], [558, 1918], [354, 1927]]}, {"text": "81", "conf": 0.665, "box": [[911, 1984], [960, 1984], [960, 2021], [911, 2021]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.854, "box": [[306, 2008], [598, 1990], [600, 2023], [308, 2041]]}]}